This function is already minimal; I only added branch-prediction hints so the two invalid-input checks (which are essentially never taken) are pushed off the hot path, leaving the field lookup straight-line.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex >= profile->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```